{"chunks":[{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000122","content":"Why Token-Prefix Continuity Breaks.\nAgent harness typically communicates with model APIs\nthrough text messages. From the harness perspective, a rollout usually consists of turn-level calls","bbox":[68.03099822998047,64.59376525878906,527.386962890625,89.7298583984375],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000123","content":"\u0001,\n(7)","bbox":[387.7439270019531,104.35218811035156,528.5209350585938,115.66417694091797],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000124","content":"Ctext(ρ) =","bbox":[199.93499755859375,102.55801391601562,247.28126525878906,115.66533660888672],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000125","content":"\u0000(ptext","bbox":[250.30499267578125,102.55801391601562,279.4184265136719,115.66533660888672],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000126","content":"2\n), . . .","bbox":[350.6079406738281,104.55360412597656,387.75396728515625,117.7289810180664],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000127","content":"2\n, atext","bbox":[324.6749572753906,102.55789184570312,365.42437744140625,117.72904205322266],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000128","content":"1\n, atext","bbox":[264.60198974609375,102.55801391601562,305.3514099121094,117.7291030883789],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000129","content":"1\n), (ptext","bbox":[290.53497314453125,102.55795288085938,339.49139404296875,117.7291030883789],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000130","content":"where the harness sends ptext","bbox":[67.63899993896484,128.83700561523438,203.66542053222656,141.3983154296875],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000131","content":"i\nand receives atext","bbox":[188.8489990234375,128.83700561523438,288.08941650390625,143.66021728515625],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000132","content":"i\n. Typically, for a multi-turn ReAct-style [16] agent,\nthe previous call forms a complete text-level prefix of the next prompt, e.g.","bbox":[68.03099822998047,130.28773498535156,528.7799682617188,155.423828125],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000133","content":"(ptext","bbox":[250.83499145507812,168.25192260742188,275.3824157714844,181.3582763671875],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000134","content":"i\n) ⪯ptext","bbox":[286.49798583984375,168.25180053710938,340.909423828125,183.4130859375],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000135","content":"i\n, atext","bbox":[260.56597900390625,168.25186157226562,301.3144226074219,183.41314697265625],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000136","content":"i+1.\n(8)","bbox":[326.0929870605469,170.2475128173828,528.5238647460938,183.42288208007812],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000137","content":"Besides, when the harness spawns subagents or summarizes its context, the training engine may\nreceive subsequent calls with different prompt histories that do not satisfy this relation.","bbox":[68.03099822998047,195.98170471191406,527.796142578125,221.11785888671875],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000138","content":"RL training operates on exact token IDs and rollout log probabilities. The RL system represents\neach call using the token sequences ptok","bbox":[68.03099822998047,224.43470764160156,527.3949584960938,249.7723388671875],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000139","content":"i\nand atok","bbox":[240.3090057373047,237.21102905273438,294.6990051269531,252.03424072265625],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000140","content":"i\n, where atok","bbox":[282.7040100097656,237.21102905273438,350.23297119140625,252.03424072265625],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000141","content":"i\n∼πθ(· | ptok","bbox":[338.23797607421875,237.21102905273438,410.0150146484375,252.03424072265625],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000142","content":"i\n). The response returned\nto the harness is atext","bbox":[68.03099822998047,238.66175842285156,527.3092651367188,263.99932861328125],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000143","content":"i\n= Decode(atok","bbox":[161.8470001220703,251.43801879882812,252.5570068359375,266.26123046875],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000144","content":"i\n). Training therefore observes the token-level sequence\nCtok(ρ) = ((ptok","bbox":[68.03099822998047,252.8887481689453,527.3831176757812,278.225341796875],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000145","content":"1 , atok\n1 ), (ptok\n2 , atok\n2 ), . . .).\nToken-prefix continuity between consecutive calls requires","bbox":[78.87901306152344,265.6650085449219,355.0538330078125,292.2508544921875],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000146","content":"\u0000ptok","bbox":[253.82000732421875,305.0790100097656,275.8700256347656,318.18634033203125],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000147","content":"\u0001 ⪯ptok","bbox":[299.6230163574219,298.828857421875,336.218017578125,318.18634033203125],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000148","content":"i\n, atok","bbox":[263.8750305175781,305.0790100097656,299.052001953125,320.24127197265625],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000149","content":"i","bbox":[287.0570068359375,312.27117919921875,289.9421691894531,320.24127197265625],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000150","content":"i+1,\n(9)","bbox":[324.2230224609375,307.07574462890625,528.5269775390625,320.2511291503906],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000151","content":"where ⪯denotes an exact token-level prefix.","bbox":[67.63900756835938,332.80877685546875,279.3846740722656,343.7779541015625],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000152","content":"In practice, Equation 8 holding does not guarantee that Equation 9 holds. The next request\nis obtained by applying a chat template and tokenizer to the updated message history. After\nretokenization, the token IDs corresponding to atext","bbox":[68.03099822998047,347.03570556640625,527.7423095703125,386.59930419921875],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000153","content":"i\ninside ptok","bbox":[308.73797607421875,374.0389709472656,378.20501708984375,388.8612060546875],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000154","content":"i+1 can differ from the originally\nsampled IDs in atok","bbox":[68.03099822998047,375.48870849609375,527.7115478515625,400.8263244628906],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000155","content":"i\n.\nThis mismatch can arise through at least three mechanisms that we observe in our study:","bbox":[78.87901306152344,389.71575927734375,507.5303955078125,414.8518371582031],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000156","content":"(1) Chat-template non-compositionality. Rendering a complete message history is not necessarily","bbox":[68.03101348876953,427.1357421875,527.76708984375,438.21392822265625],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000157","content":"equivalent to concatenating the renderings of its parts:","bbox":[87.42500305175781,441.36273193359375,349.0361633300781,452.2718505859375],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000158","content":"Template(A ∥B)̸ = Template(A) ∥Template(B).\n(10)","bbox":[191.69500732421875,467.09576416015625,528.58984375,478.2063293457031],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000159","content":"A template may insert delimiters or connecting newlines at message boundaries, or omit\nmarkers that appeared in the original generation. In practice, for example, we find that\nQwen’s chat template can remove an earlier <think> marker, breaking token-prefix continuity.","bbox":[87.02200317382812,492.8297119140625,529.4564208984375,532.9598388671875],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000160","content":"(2) Decode–retokenize drift. Token decoding is not injective, so converting sampled tokens to","bbox":[68.03099822998047,544.4757080078125,527.4420776367188,555.5965576171875],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000161","content":"text and tokenizing that text again need not recover the original token IDs:","bbox":[87.42500305175781,558.7027587890625,448.8108215332031,569.6118774414062],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000162","content":"Tok","bbox":[244.906005859375,584.4357299804688,263.09149169921875,595.3448486328125],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000163","content":"\u0000Decode(atok","bbox":[263.2070007324219,582.4400024414062,324.4749755859375,595.5463256835938],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000164","content":"\u0001̸ = atok","bbox":[329.28900146484375,576.1297607421875,366.1620178222656,595.5463256835938],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000165","content":"i\n)","bbox":[312.47998046875,584.4357299804688,329.2896423339844,597.6012573242188],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000166","content":"i\n.\n(11)","bbox":[354.1670227050781,584.4357299804688,528.52685546875,597.6012573242188],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000167","content":"Figure 3 gives a concrete example: the word having is sampled as the two tokens h and\naving, but retokenizing the same text inside a later prompt may instead produce hav and ing.\nAlthough the decoded text is unchanged, the token boundaries differ and break token-level\ncontinuity between the two calls.","bbox":[87.02200317382812,610.1697387695312,529.363037109375,663.7588500976562],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000168","content":"(3) Inference-time output transformation. Tool-call and structured-output handlers may parse,","bbox":[68.031005859375,676.042724609375,528.9185791015625,687.1494140625],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000169","content":"normalize, repair, and reserialize a sampled response before returning it to the harness. Such\nprocessing can change whitespace, delimiters, JSON structure, or invalid syntax, so the\nresponse incorporated into a later prompt may differ even at the text level from the response\nrepresented by the sampled token IDs.","bbox":[87.42500305175781,690.2697143554688,527.458740234375,743.8588256835938],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000170","content":"Mitigating Broken Token-Prefix Continuity.\nThe most direct strategy is to train every model","bbox":[68.03099822998047,762.437744140625,527.3751831054688,773.5562133789062],"section":"2.1 Retokenization and Sample Merging","page":5,"page_width":595.2760009765625,"page_height":841.8900146484375},{"id":"chunk-paper-7ca1c77cfaa945e9-000171","content":"5","bbox":[295.1449890136719,792.835998535